WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:04.690
The temperature of our favorite time of year.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.220
The sight of the landscape of the environment
we grew up in.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.800
The taste of a home cooked meal.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:19.070
The emotion of an old song that we once listened
to on repeat for a month straight.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:25.730
All of these things elicit a feeling so unique
and powerful that it appears to transcend

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.250
time and space.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:33.789
It brings us into a state of being that cannot
be described with anything other than just

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:35.789
this one word.

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:39.109
It is nostalgia.

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:44.800
Nostalgia is one of the most unique and valuable
capacities of the human mind.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.299
It is the closest thing we have to time travel.

00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:55.879
It gives us an opportunity to experience moments
of our life while being completely free from

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:59.549
our normal anxieties and uncertainties.

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:07.640
In general, every moment in life carries with
it a set of fears, anxieties, and stresses.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:15.229
We are always concerned with making the next
moment perfect and we worry about what tomorrow

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:18.000
may or may not bring.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.250
But nostalgia frees us from this.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:28.979
When we experience nostalgia, we are given
an opportunity to feel a moment as it truly

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:33.990
was, void of any fear or uncertainty.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:39.499
This is because the circumstances that we
were worried about at the time have already

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.499
past.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:48.030
At the time, our worries lied in the uncertainty
of what the next several days, months, or

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.020
years would bring.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.969
But those days have since past.

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:58.520
We have lived through the times that we were
worried about and here we are, doing just

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.070
fine.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:06.660
Ironically, letting the state of nostalgia
carry us into the past can remind us of the

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.750
importance of appreciating the present.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:19.030
It shows us that our desire to perfect all
the moments of life is foolish and unnecessary.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:26.599
It shows us that our fears and worries regarding
the future are irrational and insignificant.

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:32.360
And it shows us that we are resilient and
adaptable and that no matter what life throws

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:40.640
at us, we can sustain and continue to create
meaningful positive moments.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:46.569
Nostalgia provides clarity in that even the
moments that may have been stressful and did

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:54.250
not seem so good at the time, can still carry
a sense of great value and appreciation when

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.510
viewed through the lens of hindsight.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:05.090
This very moment in time, despite if there
are things going on that may seem negative

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:12.829
or stressful, will likely still have a feeling
of nostalgia attached to it when you are reminded

00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:15.090
of it in the future.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:47.499
And if this is true, why not appreciate it
right now as well?

